examples.question_text:
For each polynomial graph, determine whether its degree is odd or even and whether its leading coefficient is positive or negative.

(a)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-2.8,0)--(2.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,<->] (0,-3)--(0,1.6) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2:2,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{-0.55*(\x*\x-1)*(\x*\x-1)+0.8});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(b)
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=10mm,y=8mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-2.8,0)--(2.8,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[black,<->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-2:2,samples=100,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{0.4*\x*(\x*\x-1)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
